          "type": "TextualBody",
          "label": "Verso",
          "value": "<p>so I cannot go over its details so as to be able to inform you. I am concerned that if your honor delays, you will miss the canal and the goods will remain blocked in Alexandria. My opinion is that you should not delay any longer, God willing. . . .</p>\n<p>I beg your honor to continue making use of my services and that you graciously forgive me, for God knows that I have to write with bandages dangling over my eyes. \u201cGod is sufficient for me, and He is the best to be trusted.\u201d 10 Marheshvan</p>",
